-- title:
--   Frobenius semilinearity of reduced series when ψ₁^r≡ψ₂ mod r
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, let $O$ and $B$ be commutative rings, and let $\psi_1,\psi_2 : O \to B$ be ring homomorphisms such that $\psi_1(x)^r - \psi_2(x)$ lies in the ideal generated by $r$ in $B$ for every $x \in O$ (here `pIdeal r B` denotes `Ideal.span {(r : B)}`). Let $\beta = (\beta_0,\beta_1)$ be a pair of formal power series in two variables over $O/rO$, i.e. an element of `Series (O ⧸ pIdeal r O)` $= \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)(O/rO)$, and assume each $\beta_i$ has vanishing constant coefficient. Write $\beta^{\psi}$ for the pair obtained by applying the induced map $O/rO \to B/rB$ on coefficients (`residueMap ψ`, the quotient map induced by $\psi$, applied coefficientwise via `Series.map`), and let $\mathrm{Frob} = (X_0^{r^1}, X_1^{r^1})$ be `Rigidified.frobSeries (B ⧸ pIdeal r B) 1`. Then, with `Series.comp ψ φ` meaning substitution of $\varphi$ into each component of $\psi$, one has the equality of pairs of power series over $B/rB$
--   $$\mathrm{Frob} \circ \beta^{\psi_1} = \beta^{\psi_2} \circ \mathrm{Frob},$$
--   that is, $(\beta_i^{\psi_1})^r = \beta_i^{\psi_2}(X_0^r, X_1^r)$ for $i = 0,1$.
--
--   This is the Frobenius-semilinearity compatibility used when re-basing a pair of two-variable series along two coefficient homomorphisms that differ by a Frobenius congruence: it says that reduction along $\psi_2$ twists the series by the $r$-power Frobenius relative to reduction along $\psi_1$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in the rigidification statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.isPiTranslate_of_isRigTransport_of_corr_relFrobenius_of_isAtkinLehnerQuotientVia`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.isPiTranslate_of_isRigTransport_of_corr_relFrobenius_of_isAtkinLehnerQuotientVia), where rigidificators of formal $O_D$-modules are transported across a relative Frobenius correspondence.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormal_frobSeries_comp_map_residueMap_eq_map_residueMap_comp_frobSeries.lean

